  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes to `ranges.mjs`\n\nRewrote `mergeRanges(ranges)` to satisfy all requirements:\n\n**Validation (throws `TypeError`):**\n- Input must be an array.\n- Each element must be a 2-element array pair.\n- Both bounds must be safe integers (`Number.isSafeInteger`).\n- `start <= end` required.\n\n**Correct merging:**\n- Copies each pair into a fresh `[start, end]` array during validation, so the input array and its pairs are never mutated.\n- Sorts by start, then end (`a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]`).\n- Merges when intervals overlap **or touch as adjacent integers** using `start <= last[1] + 1` (so `[2,4]` + `[5,7]` → `[2,7]`).\n- Contained intervals don't shorten the current interval: the end is only extended when `end > last[1]`.\n- Returns a fresh result array of fresh pair arrays, sorted by start.\n- Empty input returns `[]`.\n\n**Preserved:** the named export `mergeRanges`.\n\nThe two provided tests (`unsorted overlaps merge in order` and `adjacent integer intervals touch`) are both satisfied by this logic.",
